"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nWe visited because we heard Sydney had a large seafood market.\n\nBut when we went to the original location shown on Google Maps, it was closed, which caught us off guard.  \nA sign said it had been renovated, but we couldn't easily find that information online.\n\nThe map on the sign pointed to the modern building right in front of us.  \nIt didn't look like a fish market at all, so we went in skeptically —  \nbut it was labeled as the fish market right on the building.\n\nInside, there were plenty of stalls selling various seafood along with a goods shop.  \nIt was more pleasant than expected, and it was quite crowded.  \nQuite a few places seemed to be having sales, probably nearing closing time.\n\nMany stalls would clean and cook the seafood right on the spot after purchase,  \nand others were set up like restaurants with ready-to-eat cooked seafood.  \nIf you're planning to eat seafood, it's worth visiting and trying the fresh catch.\n\nPrices seemed to be on par with back home in Korea.  \nThat said, king crab and snow crab seemed a bit cheaper than in Korea.  \n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"